{
  "_notes": [
    "Hook [Data East, 1992]",
    "2026-02-13 added by Tom Collins <tom@scorbit.io>",
    "Adjustments 0x1E00-0x1E67 are protected by a plain 8-bit sum (checksum8_sum, not complemented) at",
    "0x1EDA, right after the custom-message text, with a change counter at 0x1EDB. Measured live on",
    "hook_501 from 998 samples: Free Play 1 -> 0 -> 1 at 0x1E04 moved the sum by -1/+1 and Balls Per",
    "Game 3 -> 5 -> 2 -> 3 at 0x1E0D moved it by +2/-3/+1. Same scheme as tmnt_200 (sum at 0x1EFE",
    "there); the sum's address follows the banner text length. Hook does not reset the machine when",
    "the operator menu is exited.",
    "The eight bytes 0x1E68-0x1E6F are the leading spaces of the custom message (0x20 x 8 = 256, invisible",
    "to an 8-bit sum), which is why a sum over 0x1E00-0x1E6F also validates; the block ends at 0x1E67.",
    "Adjustments 0x1E00-0x1E67 are protected by a plain 8-bit sum (complement false) at 0x1EDA; see README.md in maps/dataeast."
  ],
